# THIS_FILE_IS_MANAGED_BY_ANSIBLE__DO_NOT_EDIT_MANUALLY
# Desktop session-management (ICE) auth - /etc/apparmor.d/abstractions/local_mixin_gui_session_manager
#
# TL;DR - include in: GUI apps that use libSM session management (the Mozilla / Chromium /
#         Electron / mpv family), UNCONDITIONALLY. Do NOT put behind apparmor_allow_x11.
#         Apps that never probe iceauth (the Qt / GTK XWayland viewers) should NOT include it.
#
# Grants:
#   - owner /run/user/*/iceauth_* r         read the ICE session-management auth cookie
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iceauth cookie for the ICE (Inter-Client Exchange) protocol. ICE is the transport under
# XSMP (X Session Management Protocol) - the session manager that saves / restores the
# session on logout / login. Toolkits using libSM open this to register with it.
#
# NOT the same as xauth (local_mixin_gui_x11), despite the similar name and shared X-era
# plumbing:
#   - xauth   authenticates to the X DISPLAY SERVER -> windows / input / clipboard / screen
#             -> high value -> gated behind apparmor_allow_x11.
#   - iceauth authenticates to the SESSION MANAGER  -> save / restore session, restart hints
#             -> low value, and used under BOTH Wayland and X11 (a session manager exists on
#                Wayland too), so it is granted UNCONDITIONALLY, never behind apparmor_allow_x11.
#
# Gating this behind apparmor_allow_x11 would deny it in Wayland sessions, where libSM still
# probes it; the EACCES (vs a clean ENOENT) can hang / error app startup. Keep it ungated.
#
# Read-only: the cookie is only ever read.

owner /run/user/*/iceauth_* r,
